# InterviewIQ Implementation Plan

This plan details the implementation of a fully functioning demo for **InterviewIQ: AI Interview Practice and Evaluation Platform**.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Choice:** We will use **H2 In-Memory Database** by default for the local demo so that it runs out-of-the-box without requiring a local Postgres database to be manually set up. Postgres remains configurable via properties.
> **Gemini API:** We will integrate Google Gemini API for generating questions and evaluating answers. To ensure it runs even without a key, we will implement a **fallback mockup mode** that generates realistic AI questions and scores if `GEMINI_API_KEY` is not provided.
> **ML Integration:** We will write a React-based MediaPipe webcam simulation directly in the browser to showcase real-time face/eye-tracking and speech indicators, backed by a Python FastAPI/Flask microservice for optional real frame analysis.

---

## Proposed Folder Structure

We will create a multi-module workspace:
1. `backend/`: Spring Boot Java application (existing, to be expanded).
2. `frontend/`: React + Vite + Vanilla CSS application (to be created).
3. `ml_service/`: Python microservice using Flask/FastAPI, OpenCV, MediaPipe, Scikit-learn (to be created).

